---
description: Check the current ITL branch through base update and Vanessa tests
agent: code
---

Use this command only from an active `itldev/*` development branch worktree.

Run the helper directly from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second Designer limit; if that limit is configured higher, raise the outer timeout too. Do not use `120000 ms` or other short defaults because the helper may launch 1C Designer/Enterprise operations.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action check-dev-branch
```

This is the single normal post-change executable gate. Do not run a separate base update first; the helper performs a cheap mode-aware suite/lint preflight, updates the branch infobase only when its source fingerprint is stale, then runs Vanessa Automation through packet `StartFeaturePlayer` in `TESTMANAGER -> TESTCLIENT` mode with a branch-local test port. It also checks the current branch file infobase event log against the branch baseline and fails on fresh non-baseline `Error` records. The compact runner returns a bounded JSON summary. Follow its `requiredAction`/`nextAction`; failed coverage or verification routes to `/itl-verify-fix`. Treat the category as a diagnostic hint, not automatic proof that the test or product is wrong. Read the last 80 lines of `logPath` only for an unclassified runner failure.
